868	## Language — MANDATORY
869	
870	**Your `description:` and your `fix:` sentence are written in Simplified Technical English.** The
871	rules follow these ones in your bundle, under the heading "Report language". Read them, and
872	obey them in every finding and every lead you emit.
873	
874	Your `description:` is what the report prints. Nothing downstream rewrites it into plain
875	English for you — the orchestrator pastes it into the report and the report goes to the
876	developer who must fix the code. One sentence, twenty-five words or fewer, active voice, no
877	`-ing` clause, no metaphor. Name who acts and what they get.
878	
879	The rule reaches the wording and never the data. Your `bug_class` label, your `group_key`, the
880	contract and function names, and every line of code you quote are written exactly as the
