920	Your `description:` is what the report prints. Nothing downstream rewrites it into plain
921	English for you — the orchestrator pastes it into the report and the report goes to the
922	developer who must fix the code. One sentence, twenty-five words or fewer, active voice, no
923	`-ing` clause, no metaphor. Name who acts and what they get.
924	
925	The rule reaches the wording and never the data. Your `bug_class` label, your `group_key`, the
926	contract and function names, and every line of code you quote are written exactly as the
927	source and the dedup rules require. `report-language.md` says which is which.
